      <pattern name="fluent-v9-component-authoring" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md">Shared-lib chrome/token conventions.</pattern>
      <pattern name="fluent-v9-react-version-boundaries" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-react-version-boundaries.md">Dual-React (18/19) safety.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load `WizardShell.tsx`, the `WizardModal` preset, `SprkModal/sizes.ts`, and the reconciled `ModalWindowControls`. Declare RIGOR: FULL.</step>
    <step order="1">Re-base the WizardShell header to the `SprkModal` standard header: title (ellipsized) on the left, `ModalWindowControls` (FullScreen glyph from task 003 + ×) on the right, standard bottom border tokens (`strokeWidthThin` / `colorNeutralStroke2`).</step>
    <step order="2">Re-base the footer to the standard footer tokens (Cancel always left via `footerStart`; Skip · Back · Next on the right) using semantic tokens only.</step>
    <step order="3">Align the shell to the named `wizard` size from `sizes.ts` (replace the ad-hoc 95vw/70vh defaults); keep the Fluent sizing-clamp fix. RETAIN the Dialog envelope, `embedded` mode, and the 200px stepper unchanged.</step>
    <step order="4">Build the shared lib; build/run every consuming `Create*`/direct wizard and confirm the aligned chrome renders and the stepper + `embedded` mode still work.</step>
    <step order="5">Rebuild the iframe web-resource bundles that embed WizardShell and confirm they are unaffected (still compile + package).</step>
    <step order="6">Confirm dual-React clean (build under `@types/react` 18 and React 19).</step>
    <step order="7">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 080 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation (e.g. a wizard that needed a size other than `wizard`, or an `embedded`-mode edge case) in `projects/spaarke-modal-system/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If aligning the header/footer/size tokens forces breaking the `embedded` envelope or forces a change inside any `Create*`/direct wizard's internals, STOP and surface it per CLAUDE.md §6 / §6.5 — light-first is the owner-chosen depth (§11-G); a deeper internal re-base is a separate decision, not something to do silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Wizard chrome matches the standard">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a representative `Create*` wizard (e.g. Create New Matter) through WizardShell.</step>
        <step>Inspect the header (title + FullScreen maximize/restore + ×) and footer (Cancel left; Skip · Back · Next right).</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Header + footer match the canonical `SprkModal` standard; window controls show the FullScreen glyph; the wizard is sized to the `wizard` named size.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Embedded mode + stepper intact">
      <steps>
        <step>Render WizardShell in `embedded` mode with the 200px stepper populated.</step>
        <step>Step forward/back through the wizard.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>`embedded` mode renders without the Dialog envelope regressions; the 200px stepper still tracks steps; no clipping.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark-mode parity (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render WizardShell under a dark FluentProvider theme.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Header/footer chrome uses semantic tokens and reads correctly in dark mode; no hardcoded color.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test shared lib and consuming wizards (build:prod for PCF/web-resource bundles)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Wizard/WizardShell.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a wizard opened via WizardShell, the header uses the standard `SprkModal` header (ellipsized title + `ModalWindowControls` FullScreen glyph + ×) and the footer uses the standard footer tokens (Cancel left; nav/actions right).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The shell is sized to the named `wizard` size from `sizes.ts` (no ad-hoc 95vw/70vh literal).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The WizardShell envelope, `embedded` mode, and the 200px stepper are retained and functional (no full internal re-base performed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All consuming `Create*`/direct wizards and the iframe web-resource builds compile and package green under `@types/react` 18 and React 19.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No hex, `'1px'` literals, or inline color styles are introduced in the re-based chrome (ADR-021 / NFR-03).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Modify-only — no `&lt;justification&gt;` (`WizardShell` already exists; this edits it). Depth is owner-locked to light-first (§11-G): tokens + size + window controls only, envelope/embedded/stepper preserved. Depends on 003 (glyph) and 008 (`SprkModal` base + `WizardModal` preset tokens). The `WizardModal` preset is the canonical reference for the target header/footer/size. COMPLETED 2026-08-02 (solo sub-agent, FULL): header/footer aligned to SprkModal tokens (ellipsized title, strokeWidthThin/colorNeutralStroke2 borders, spacing S/L); footer reordered Skip·Back·Next w/ transparent Skip (matches WizardModal); default size = getSurfaceStyle('wizard') (95vw/70vh literals gone); maxWidth/height override contract + embedded + 200px stepper + envelope 100% unchanged (061's FindSimilar xl overrides proven intact). 9-consumer matrix green across React 16/18/19: UI.Components (full suite at exact baseline), AI.Widgets, SemanticSearchControl build:prod (transitively bundles WizardShell via DocumentEmailWizard — non-obvious blast-radius finding), SpaarkeAi, DocumentUploadWizard, SpeAdminApp, external-spa (React 18); LW via scoped tsc (#712). Zero consumer-file changes needed; zero escalations. Discovered pre-existing LW WorkAssignmentWizardDialog FORK → Issue #715 / DEF-004. Detail: notes/task-080-completion.md.</notes>

  <execution>
